[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2600968562","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101800#issuecomment-2600968562","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101800","id":2600968562,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bB6Fy","user":{"login":"BaconEggsRL","id":18596035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk2MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18596035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL","html_url":"https://github.com/BaconEggsRL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-19T18:18:11Z","updated_at":"2025-01-19T18:19:03Z","body":"Ok, I still can't seem to figure out exactly what causes this, but the solution for me was to make sure I was emitting the \"toggled\" signal instead of the \"pressed\" signal if trying to press a button in the group via code.\nI tried making an example project but couldn't replicate the behavior I was seeing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2600968562/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218151541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101800#issuecomment-3218151541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101800","id":3218151541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_0Rh1","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T14:25:47Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T14:25:47Z","body":"Can't replicate either in a simple scene. But as you mention, if you're triggering buttons through code, manually firing their signals is not the best way to do that. Godot uses those signals internally to propagate button presses and there's specific logic tied to both `pressed` and `toggled` signals for the correct behavior in button groups. Messing with those signals' emission order/count can mess things up.\n\nAlways use public API (e.g. [`button_pressed`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/classes/class_basebutton.html#class-basebutton-property-button-pressed)) whenever possible.\n\nIf this fixes the issue in your project, then I'd say this is not a bug.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218151541/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6282708794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101800#issuecomment-6282708794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101800","id":6282708794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdnqHOg","user":{"login":"BaconEggsRL","id":18596035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk2MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18596035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL","html_url":"https://github.com/BaconEggsRL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T03:33:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T03:33:48Z","body":"> 4\\. Can't replicate either in a simple scene. But as you mention, if you're triggering buttons through code, manually firing their signals is not the best way to do that. Godot uses those signals internally to propagate button presses and there's specific logic tied to both `pressed` and `toggled` signals for the correct behavior in button groups. Messing with those signals' emission order/count can mess things up.\n>     Always use public API (e.g. [`button_pressed`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/classes/class_basebutton.html#class-basebutton-property-button-pressed)) whenever possible.\n>     If this fixes the issue in your project, then I'd say this is not a bug.\n\nAgreed; I think the issue was caused by emitting signals.\nThe correct way to do this in code seems to be to assign a ```button_pressed``` value.\nThis automatically triggers unpressing the other buttons in the button group.\nAlso ```set_pressed_no_signal``` exists if you don't want to trigger the signal path.\n\nClosing as not planned.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6282708794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]